# FF 3h, review on PR 287: on a volume (no accounts, HOME=/home), `ln -s notes/a.txt link` in /home/rs, then Index's
# Move to Trash from the keyed menu (Shift+F10; Up to the strip, Right to its last slot, Trash). `finder --trash`
# lists the link: in the trash it points nowhere, and a link to nothing is listed as itself. The check line typed
# last ends the session with status 0: the link is in .trash/items with its record, and gone from /home/rs.
hdesk: screen 1920x1080 plane 1920x
~hdesk: bar desktop 1 \|Index\| var \|/home/rs\|.*
finder: filter |link| items 1
finder: menu FILE at 
=finder: menu chose |Trash|
=finder: trash |/home/rs/link| (0)
=hdesk: pixel 1 ended
=finder: dir |/home/.trash/items| items 1 folders 0 files 1
=hdesk: pixel 1 ended
=hdesk: shell ended, status 0
